{=============================================================================
  Entropy change of water in a two-compartment rigid tank
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0172
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  A rigid tank is split into two equal hermetic compartments. One holds
  2.5 kg of compressed liquid water at 400 kPa and 60 °C; the other is
  under vacuum. After the partition is removed the pressure is 40 kPa.
  The model computes the entropy change of the water. Exercise 7 of
  repetition R4, ULiège MECA0002, 2022-2023.

  Inputs : p1, T1, m, p2
  Outputs: DELTAS, s1, s2, x1, x2, v1, v2
  Units  : SI - temperatures in °C, pressures in Pa, energies in J
  Source : S. Quoilin, ULiège MECA0002, 2022-2023 - see README.md
=============================================================================}

"!Exercise 7 (English paraphrase of the original French statement)"
"A rigid tank is divided into two hermetic parts of equal volume. One part is filled with 2.5 kg of compressed
 liquid water at 400 kPa and 60 C; the other is under vacuum. The two parts are then connected and the pressure
 falls to 40 kPa. Calculate the entropy change of this process."

"!Inputs"
p1 = 400e3 [Pa]   "initial pressure of the water [Pa]; 400 kPa in the original"
p2 = 40e3 [Pa]    "pressure after the compartments are connected [Pa]; 40 kPa in the original"
T1 = 60 [C]       "initial temperature of the water [°C]"
m = 2.5 [kg]      "mass of water [kg]; 2,5 in the original"

"!Initial state: compressed liquid in one compartment"
v1 = volume(Water, P=p1, T=T1)    "specific volume of the water [m^3/kg]"
s1 = entropy(Water, P=p1, T=T1)   "specific entropy of the water [J/kg-K]"
x1 = quality(Water, P=p1, T=T1)   "quality, to check that the water is liquid [-]"

"!Final specific volume: the two compartment volumes are equal"
v2 = 2*v1                         "final specific volume [m^3/kg]; the empty compartment has the same volume"

"!Final state at the given pressure and the final specific volume"
s2 = entropy(Water, P=p2, v=v2)   "final specific entropy [J/kg-K]"
x2 = quality(Water, P=p2, v=v2)   "final quality [-]"

"!Entropy change of the water"
DELTAS = m*(s2 - s1)              "entropy change of the process [J/K]"

"!State points for the thermodynamic diagrams (post-processing, no effect on the results)"
{1: water before the partition is removed. 2: water after the compartments are connected.}
P[1] = p1                                      "initial pressure [Pa]"
h[1] = enthalpy(Water, P=p1, T=T1)             "initial enthalpy [J/kg]"
T[1] = T1                                      "initial temperature [°C]"
s[1] = s1                                      "initial entropy [J/kg-K]"
P[2] = p2                                      "final pressure [Pa]"
h[2] = enthalpy(Water, P=p2, v=v2)             "final enthalpy [J/kg]"
T[2] = temperature(Water, P=p2, v=v2)          "final temperature [°C]"
s[2] = s2                                      "final entropy [J/kg-K]"
